{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789405848,"nonce":"lJZMRSae1qfvfHB0qt9Q9CA/jcs=","title":"Python: tuples of settled shape as value structs","message":"`(x, y) = pairs[i]`, `points.append((x, y))`, dict items, `zip` pairs:\na tuple is a boxed `List\u003cAny\u003e` under a tag, so a pair is three\nallocations and its elements are boxes, and every unpack is two box\nreads. bench_pipeline.py's `[(x % 1000, x) for x in evens]` and the\nkeyed sort over it pay this per element.\n\nFix: a tuple literal of known arity whose element kinds are settled by\ninference is a value struct (unboxed, stack or inline in a typed\n`List\u003c(Int, Int)\u003e`), the way `list[Body]` became a list of instances;\nunpacking is field reads, indexing by constant is a field read, and\nequality and ordering are lexicographic over the fields. A tuple that\nmust become `Any` (stored in a `List\u003cAny\u003e`, passed to a dynamic\ncallee) is boxed at that point, as an instance is.","files":null}]}